I can't think of a good solution for that problem right now without forking the library, the concept of min and max encodes both the visual and filter range. What I can think of is transforming the response to filter out the outliers instead of setting min and max:

```
const originalSearch = searchClient.search;
searchClient.search = function (requests) {
  return originalSearch(requests).then(({ results }) => ({
    results: results.map((result) => {
      if (!result.facets_stats || !result.facets_stats.price) {
        return result;
      }

      return {
        ...result,
        facets_stats: {
          ...result.facets_stats,
          price: {
            ...result.facets_stats.price,
            // override the maximum
            max: 2000,
          },
        },
      };
    }),
  }));
};
```

